<h1 style="text-align: start; line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 26px; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="start"><strong>Dodge, Tuttle and Driving Park Pools will not open Saturday and Sunday </strong></h1>
<h2 style="text-align: start; line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #CB343C; font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="start">Pools will open Monday, May 31</h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">Because you signed up for a time slot for one of the City’s pools this weekend, we wanted to inform you that Dodge, Tuttle and Driving Parks pools will not open Saturday as scheduled. Due to Saturday's high temperature of 55 degrees, <strong>the pools will not open until Monday, May 31.</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">The spray parks at Linden, Blackburn, Barnett and Scioto Southland community centers also will remain closed until Monday.</p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">While we wish we didn’t have to close the pools on Saturday and Sunday, swimming isn’t a safe or enjoyable activity in the unseasonable temperatures expected this weekend.</p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">We look forward to seeing you on Monday, May 31, and throughout the summer! Make sure to sign up at <a href="https://www.columbus.gov/pools/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">columbus.gov/pools</a> for another time slot.</p>
